ALTER TABLE
DIfferent Scenarios:

a)Add column
ALTER TABLE users
ADD COLUMN is_active BOOLEAN DEFAULT TRUE;

b)Drop column
ALTER TABLE users
DROP COLUMN is_active;

c)Change datatype/properties
ALTER TABLE users
MODIFY COLUMN name VARCHAR(150);

Remember:

MODIFY COLUMN changes the definition of an existing column.
MODIFY COLUMN
    column_name
    new_datatype
    desired_properties;

d)Change column name

Use:

ALTER TABLE users
CHANGE COLUMN name full_name VARCHAR(150);

Notice something important:

CHANGE COLUMN requires the old name + new name + datatype.

e)Change column position
ALTER TABLE users
MODIFY COLUMN email VARCHAR(150) AFTER id;

or:

ALTER TABLE users
MODIFY COLUMN email VARCHAR(150) FIRST;

---------imp:
Remember:
You cannot check NULL with:
WHERE email = NULL
❌ Wrong.

Use:
WHERE email IS NULL;
or:
WHERE email IS NOT NULL;
